experiment: hcsweep
  instrument        hcsweep   trial seed 0000000001356b97   1214 trials per arm
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  hcsweep -- is there an operating point where the GESTURE and the
  LESSON both work? The gesture is free and replicated; the lesson is
  free and measured; at the one point where the gesture was tuned, the
  lesson keeps only a fifth of its strength.
  the quantity  per gain, TWO numbers: error early-minus-late on a FIXED
                target (the lesson), and the phase separation with its
                share (the gesture). Both have to be read or the trade is
                invisible.
  the bar       fixed in advance: some gain must give a lesson drop over
                HALF of the half-centre-off reference 0.2197 -- that is
                0.1099 -- while keeping sep > 10 Hz and share in 0.15-0.85.
  refused if    no gain clears both at once. That is not another refused
                mechanism: it says the two do not COMPOSE at any operating
                point, which is a statement about the architecture.
  liveness      `voiced` is the voiced frame fraction. A gain outside the
                oscillating window silences the voice, and a silent
                creature has no lesson to lose -- so a null there is a
                BOUND on the window, not a failure of teaching.


  gain   arm        n  lesson drop (early-late) sep (ph1-ph0)       share    off voiced
  0.15   fixed     18  +0.2062 +/- 0.0079     (no phase bins)      0.00   0.00   0.67
  0.15   phase     18  -0.0004 +/- 0.0014     +3.2 +/- 0.1 Hz      0.49   0.00   0.69
  0.30   fixed     18  +0.1835 +/- 0.0062     (no phase bins)      0.00   0.00   0.67
  0.30   phase     18  +0.0003 +/- 0.0013     +3.6 +/- 0.1 Hz      0.50   0.00   0.69
  0.45   fixed     18  +0.1243 +/- 0.0095     (no phase bins)      0.00   0.00   0.67
  0.45   phase     18  -0.0008 +/- 0.0014     +8.0 +/- 0.1 Hz      0.49   0.00   0.68
  0.60   fixed     18  +0.0465 +/- 0.0073     (no phase bins)      0.00   0.00   0.67
  0.60   phase     18  -0.0009 +/- 0.0015     +19.5 +/- 0.3 Hz     0.50   0.00   0.67

  the half-centre-off reference for this quantity is +0.2197, and the
  previous measurement at gain 0.60 was +0.0465. A gain-0.60 row far from
  that second number means the comparison itself is broken.

  THE TRADE, gain by gain (lesson from the fixed arm, gesture from the
  phase arm at the same gain)
    gain 0.15   lesson +0.2062 OK    gesture sep   +3.2 share 0.49 no    
    gain 0.30   lesson +0.1835 OK    gesture sep   +3.6 share 0.50 no    
    gain 0.45   lesson +0.1243 OK    gesture sep   +8.0 share 0.49 no    
    gain 0.60   lesson +0.0465 no    gesture sep  +19.5 share 0.50 OK    

  THEY DO NOT COMPOSE AT ANY GAIN IN THE WINDOW. The best lesson over the
  sweep is +0.2062 at gain 0.15 against a bar of 0.1099, and where the lesson
  is strongest the gesture is weakest. This is not one more refused
  mechanism: both parts work separately and measurably, and the claim is
  that THIS ARCHITECTURE cannot run them at once -- a scalar reward writing
  into a rate-weighted centroid that a mutual-inhibition attractor is
  already holding at one of its two ends.

  WHAT WOULD OVERTURN IT: a gain outside the swept range that is still
  inside the oscillating window, or the same sweep in `halfcenter_drive`,
  which is the axis the window was actually mapped in.
